  <TITLE>
    <TI>
      <NO.DOC.C>(2004/C 84 E/0572)</NO.DOC.C>
      <P>WRITTEN QUESTION E-2526/03</P>
      <P>by Nicholas Clegg (ELDR) to the Commission</P>
      <P>(<DATE ISO="20030729">29 July 2003</DATE>)</P>
    </TI>
  </TITLE>
  <CONTENTS>
    <GR.SEQ LEVEL="1">
      <TITLE>
        <TI>
          <NP>
            <NO.P>
              <HT TYPE="ITALIC">Subject:</HT>
            </NO.P>
            <TXT>EU egg producers</TXT>
          </NP>
        </TI>
      </TITLE>
      <GR.SEQ LEVEL="2">
        <P>Is the Commission aware of the acute concerns amongst egg producers in the European Union over the threat to their livelihoods from a combination of new legislation on the welfare of hens and the potential increase of egg imports under the terms of the ongoing WTO round?</P>
        <P>What steps are being taken by the European Commission to ensure a level playing field in the international trade in eggs and in providing adequate compensation to European Union egg producers?</P>
      </GR.SEQ>
      <GR.SEQ LEVEL="2">
        <TITLE>
          <TI>
            <P>Answer given by Mr Fischler on behalf of the Commission</P>
            <P>
              <HT TYPE="ITALIC">
                <HT TYPE="NORMAL">(<DATE ISO="20030912">12 September 2003</DATE>)</HT>
              </HT>
            </P>
          </TI>
        </TITLE>
        <P>The Commission would refer the Honourable Member to its answer to written E-l625/03 by Mrs Jackson<NOTE NOTE.ID="E0001" NUMBERING="ARAB" TYPE="CHAPTER">
            <P>
              <REF.DOC.OJ COLL="C" NO.OJ="033E" DATE.PUB="20040206" PAGE.FIRST="147">OJ C 33 E, 6.2.2004, p. 147</REF.DOC.OJ>.</P>
          </NOTE>
        </P>
      </GR.SEQ>
    </GR.SEQ>
  </CONTENTS>
